      "content": "interesting. i was reading a case study about how some clinicians actually assume certain diseases are less likely in non-white patients because they don't fit the \"classic\" textbook description. for something like systemic lupus or even certain types of cardiovascular issues, do you think there's a tendency to overlook them in minority groups because their symptoms don't match the \"standard\" way these diseases are taught?",
